<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms FormNewProfile — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — "Create New Profile" dialog (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual-parity reimplementation of the WinForms `Forms/Profiles/FormNewProfile`
    (FormNewProfile.cs + FormNewProfile.Designer.cs). It prompts the operator for a new
    environment-profile name and lets them choose what to copy the new profile FROM: a fresh
    "<Empty Profile>" reset, the current profile, or any existing *.xml profile in the
    environment directory. Per AAP §0.3.3 this is a faithful parity reimplementation of the
    currently rendered Windows Forms UI — never a redesign: no new colours, no relayout, no UX
    changes. Every size, font and colour below is taken verbatim from FormNewProfile.Designer.cs.

    WINDOW SHELL — mirrors FormNewProfile.Designer.cs exactly:
      Text "Create New Profile"   -> Title (runtime gStr.gsCreateNewProfile is assigned by the
                                     code-behind; hidden by the borderless shell but kept for
                                     taskbar / automation).
      ClientSize 637 x 390        -> Width / Height (SystemDecorations="None" => client == window;
                                     MinWidth=650 clamps the effective start width to 650, exactly
                                     as the WinForms MinimumSize 650 x 370 over-rode the 637 client).
      BackColor WhiteSmoke        -> Background="#FFF5F5F5" (WinForms Color.WhiteSmoke == #FFF5F5F5).
                                     Hard-coded for parity and intentionally theme-independent —
                                     like the sibling utility dialogs (FormInputDialogView /
                                     FormEventViewerView) — so App.axaml's day/night brushes are
                                     NOT consumed here. App.axaml's FluentTheme still supplies the
                                     default TextBox / Button / ListBox control templates.
      ControlBox = false          -> covered by the borderless (SystemDecorations="None") shell +
                                     a 1px root Border; the dialog is dismissed only via its own
                                     in-window Cancel / Create buttons (sibling-dialog convention).
      MinimumSize 650 x 370       -> MinWidth="650" MinHeight="370".
      (default Sizable border)    -> CanResize="True" (the designer never set FormBorderStyle, so
                                     the WinForms default — a sizable window — is preserved).
      ShowInTaskbar = false       -> ShowInTaskbar="False".
      StartPosition.CenterParent  -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner" (shown owned over FormGPS).
      Font Tahoma 14.25pt         -> FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="19" (14.25pt x 96/72 = 19 DIP).
      (NOT TopMost — the designer never set TopMost, so this dialog is intentionally not topmost.)

    WIRING CONTRACT — this view is a CODE-BEHIND dialog, NOT MVVM (exactly like the sibling
    FormInputDialogView / FormFilePickerView):
      * There is intentionally NO DataContext and NO {Binding} to a view-model. The partner
        code-behind (FormNewProfileView.axaml.cs, partial class
        AgOpenGPS.Views.Profiles.FormNewProfileView : Window) owns ALL behaviour and addresses
        every control imperatively BY x:Name. The x:Names below MUST stay exactly as written —
        the code-behind references each one: labelName, textBoxName, labelCopyFrom,
        listViewProfiles, buttonCancel, textCancel, buttonCreate, textCreate.
      * Event handlers wired here as XAML attributes (the code-behind defines matching handlers,
        reproducing the WinForms Designer's `this.ctrl.Event += ...` wiring):
            textBoxName.Tapped       -> TextBoxName_Tapped        (WinForms textBoxName_Click: shows
                                        the on-screen keyboard when isKeyboardOn and no job started).
            textBoxName.TextChanged  -> TextBoxName_TextChanged    (WinForms textBoxName_TextChanged:
                                        glm.fileRegex sanitisation + enables buttonCreate when the
                                        name is non-empty).
            buttonCancel.Click       -> ButtonCancel_Click         (WinForms DialogResult.Cancel).
            buttonCreate.Click       -> ButtonCreate_Click         (WinForms buttonOK_Click /
                                        DialogResult.OK — creates the profile).
      * The translated caption strings are assigned at runtime by the code-behind
        (FormNewProfile_Load): labelName = gStr.gsName + ":", labelCopyFrom = gStr.gsCopyFrom + ":",
        textCreate = gStr.gsCreate, textCancel = gStr.gsCancel. The literal strings below are the
        designer's design-time placeholders.
      * buttonCreate starts DISABLED (WinForms buttonCreate.Enabled = false) -> IsEnabled="False";
        the code-behind re-enables it from TextBoxName_TextChanged once a name is typed.

    THE "COPY FROM" LIST (listViewProfiles):
      WinForms used a Details ListView with HeaderStyle=None and two columns — "Profiles" (Width
      450) and an unlabelled current-marker column (Width 150) — FullRowSelect, MultiSelect=false,
      HideSelection=false, BackColor InactiveCaption, Tahoma 18pt Bold. Avalonia has no Details
      ListView, so this is an Avalonia ListBox (SelectionMode="Single") whose ItemTemplate renders
      the same two columns. The code-behind fills listViewProfiles with a small item type exposing
      `Display` (column 1 — the profile name, e.g. "<Empty Profile>" or a *.xml file name) and
      `CurrentMarker` (column 2 — "(current)" for the active profile, otherwise empty). Because this
      is a code-behind dialog with NO x:DataType, the two {Binding Display} / {Binding CurrentMarker}
      slots are classic REFLECTION bindings against that item object; the root therefore sets
      x:CompileBindings="False" (the canonical opt-out, as in the sibling FormFilePickerView) so the
      template binds regardless of the project's compiled-bindings default. This binds to the item
      object only — there is no view-model involved.

    Button glyphs are served from the GPS assembly via avares:// URIs
    (avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/{Cancel64,OK64}.png — both 64 x 64 on disk), matching the file
    casing and the avares:// convention already used by the sibling GPS views.

    No System.Windows.Forms, no OpenTK, no Win32 / Windows-only types are referenced — Avalonia
    11.3 markup only.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.Profiles.FormNewProfileView"
        x:CompileBindings="False"
        Title="Create New Profile"
        Width="637"
        Height="390"
        MinWidth="650"
        MinHeight="370"
        Background="{DynamicResource AogLegacyWhiteSmokeBrush}"
        SystemDecorations="None"
        CanResize="True"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        FontFamily="Tahoma"
        FontSize="19">

    <Window.Styles>
        <!--
            Shared flat / transparent image-button face. The WinForms buttons were FlatStyle.Flat
            with FlatAppearance.BorderSize = 0 and an image-over-caption face on the WhiteSmoke form.
            This class reproduces that: a transparent, border-less button that stays transparent
            through pointerover / pressed (the Fluent Button template otherwise paints its own
            hover / press fill over the flat face). The pointerover / pressed setters target the
            Fluent template's content presenter — the same technique used by the sibling
            FormFilePickerView / FormRecordPickerView and Keypad/NumKeypad.axaml. ContentAlignment is
            stretched so the inner image+caption Grid fills the whole 80 x 92 button face.
        -->
        <Style Selector="Button.flatBtn">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatBtn:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatBtn:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <!--
            Keep the flat face transparent in the DISABLED state too. buttonCreate starts disabled
            (WinForms buttonCreate.Enabled = false), and the Fluent Button template otherwise paints
            a grey disabled fill over the flat face — WinForms instead left the disabled button's
            background transparent (only the glyph greys out). This override restores that parity.
        -->
        <Style Selector="Button.flatBtn:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>

        <!--
            Tighten the Fluent ListBoxItem to the WinForms ListView row rhythm: no extra item
            min-height / corner radius and stretch the row content full width so the selection
            highlight spans the whole row (WinForms FullRowSelect = true, HideSelection = false).
        -->
        <Style Selector="ListBox#listViewProfiles ListBoxItem">
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="2,1" />
            <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!--
        ControlBox=false -> borderless shell. A 1px neutral-grey root Border draws the window edge
        (the sibling-dialog convention) since SystemDecorations="None" removes the OS frame.
    -->
    <Border BorderBrush="#FF808080" BorderThickness="1">

        <!--
            The WinForms form is a resizable window whose controls use Anchors: the name textbox
            anchors Top/Left/Right (stretches horizontally), the "copy from" list anchors all four
            sides (fills the centre), and the two command buttons anchor Bottom/Right. A Grid
            reproduces that anchor behaviour faithfully and reflows on resize:
              Row 0 (64) — name label + textbox    (designer: label @ y25, textbox @ y20 h33)
              Row 1 (38) — "copy from" label        (designer: label @ y68)            => list top y102
              Row 2 (*)  — the profile list         (designer: list @ y102, h166)      => fills centre
              Row 3 (Auto) — bottom-right buttons    (designer: buttons @ y268, 80x92)
            64 + 38 + (92 + 30 bottom) = 224 fixed, so at the 390 design height the list resolves to
            166 px — identical to the WinForms list height.
        -->
        <Grid>
            <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                <RowDefinition Height="64" />
                <RowDefinition Height="38" />
                <RowDefinition Height="*" />
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            </Grid.RowDefinitions>

            <!--
                Row 0 — name row. A 150 / * column split: the right-aligned label occupies the first
                150 px (its text right edge lands at x≈150, the WinForms label's right edge) and the
                textbox fills the rest. textBoxName Margin "10,0,42,0" reproduces the designer gap
                (textbox left x160 = 150 + 10) and its 42 px right inset (637 client - 595 textbox
                right edge), so at the 637 design width the textbox is 435 px wide — its designer Size.
            -->
            <Grid Grid.Row="0" ColumnDefinitions="150,*">
                <!-- labelName: WinForms Label (15,25) 135x23, Tahoma 14.25pt Bold, ForeColor Black,
                     TextAlign MiddleRight. Runtime text = gStr.gsName + ":" (placeholder below). -->
                <TextBlock x:Name="labelName"
                           Grid.Column="0"
                           Text="Name:"
                           FontFamily="Tahoma"
                           FontSize="19"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           Foreground="Black"
                           TextAlignment="Right"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                           VerticalAlignment="Center" />

                <!-- textBoxName: WinForms TextBox (160,20) 435x33, anchor Top/Left/Right, BackColor
                     White, Tahoma 15.75pt (= 21 DIP). Tapped -> on-screen keyboard; TextChanged ->
                     filename sanitisation + enable Create (both handled in the code-behind). -->
                <TextBox x:Name="textBoxName" AutomationProperties.Name="New profile name"
                         Grid.Column="1"
                         Margin="10,0,42,0"
                         Height="33"
                         Background="White"
                         FontFamily="Tahoma"
                         FontSize="21"
                         VerticalAlignment="Center"
                         VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                         Tapped="TextBoxName_Tapped"
                         TextChanged="TextBoxName_TextChanged" />
            </Grid>

            <!-- Row 1 — labelCopyFrom: WinForms Label (15,68) 135x23, Tahoma 14.25pt Bold, ForeColor
                 Black, TextAlign MiddleRight. Pinned left at the same x15 / 135-wide column as
                 labelName so the two captions align. Runtime text = gStr.gsCopyFrom + ":". -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="labelCopyFrom"
                       Grid.Row="1"
                       Text="Copy from:"
                       Width="135"
                       Margin="15,0,0,0"
                       FontFamily="Tahoma"
                       FontSize="19"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       Foreground="Black"
                       TextAlignment="Right"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center" />

            <!--
                Row 2 — listViewProfiles: the "copy from" list. WinForms ListView (Details,
                HeaderStyle=None) @ (13,102) 611x166, BackColor InactiveCaption (~#FFBFCDDB),
                Tahoma 18pt Bold (= 24 DIP), FullRowSelect, MultiSelect=false, HideSelection=false.
                Avalonia ListBox: Background #FFBFCDDB, SelectionMode="Single", BorderThickness 0
                (the root Border already frames the dialog). Margin "13,0,13,0" reproduces the
                designer's 13 px left inset and matching right inset (list right edge x624 of the
                637 client). The horizontal scrollbar is disabled (LabelWrap=false / single line).
                ItemsSource and the item objects (Display / CurrentMarker) are supplied by the
                code-behind.
            -->
            <ListBox x:Name="listViewProfiles" AutomationProperties.Name="Copy-from profile list"
                     Grid.Row="2"
                     Margin="13,0,13,0"
                     Background="#FFBFCDDB"
                     BorderThickness="0"
                     FontFamily="Tahoma"
                     FontSize="24"
                     FontWeight="Bold"
                     SelectionMode="Single"
                     ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled">
                <ListBox.ItemTemplate>
                    <DataTemplate>
                        <!--
                            One row = two columns matching the WinForms ColumnHeader widths
                            (Profiles 450 / current-marker 150). NO x:DataType is set (code-behind
                            dialog), so {Binding Display} / {Binding CurrentMarker} are classic
                            reflection bindings against the item object the code-behind supplies —
                            the only bindings in this file, and no view-model is involved.
                        -->
                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="450,150">
                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="0"
                                       Text="{Binding Display}"
                                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                       TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="1"
                                       Text="{Binding CurrentMarker}"
                                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                       TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
                        </Grid>
                    </DataTemplate>
                </ListBox.ItemTemplate>
            </ListBox>

            <!--
                Row 3 — bottom-right command buttons. WinForms: buttonCancel @ (461,268) 80x92 then
                buttonCreate @ (546,268) 80x92, both anchored Bottom/Right. Reproduced as a
                right-aligned horizontal StackPanel (Cancel first, Create second — designer order)
                with Spacing 5 (the 5 px designer gap: 546 - 541) and a 11 px right / 30 px bottom
                inset (buttons right edge x626 of the 637 client; 390 - 360 button bottom = 30).
                Each button: a flat/transparent face with the 64 px glyph on top (WinForms
                ImageAlign TopCenter) and the caption beneath (WinForms TextAlign BottomCenter).
            -->
            <StackPanel Grid.Row="3"
                        Orientation="Horizontal"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                        VerticalAlignment="Top"
                        Margin="0,0,11,30"
                        Spacing="5">

                <!-- buttonCancel: WinForms DialogResult.Cancel, image Cancel64, caption "Cancel"
                     (runtime gStr.gsCancel via textCancel). -->
                <Button x:Name="buttonCancel"
                        Classes="flatBtn"
                        Width="80"
                        Height="92"
                        Click="ButtonCancel_Click"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Cancel">
                    <Grid RowDefinitions="Auto,*">
                        <Image Grid.Row="0"
                               Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/Cancel64.png"
                               Width="64"
                               Height="64"
                               Stretch="Uniform"
                               HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                               VerticalAlignment="Top" />
                        <TextBlock x:Name="textCancel"
                                   Grid.Row="1"
                                   Text="Cancel"
                                   FontFamily="Tahoma"
                                   FontSize="19"
                                   HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                   VerticalAlignment="Bottom" />
                    </Grid>
                </Button>

                <!-- buttonCreate: WinForms DialogResult.OK (buttonOK_Click), image OK64, caption
                     "Create" (runtime gStr.gsCreate via textCreate). Starts DISABLED; the
                     code-behind enables it once a non-empty name is typed. -->
                <Button x:Name="buttonCreate"
                        Classes="flatBtn"
                        Width="80"
                        Height="92"
                        IsEnabled="False"
                        Click="ButtonCreate_Click"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Create">
                    <Grid RowDefinitions="Auto,*">
                        <Image Grid.Row="0"
                               Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/OK64.png"
                               Width="64"
                               Height="64"
                               Stretch="Uniform"
                               HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                               VerticalAlignment="Top" />
                        <TextBlock x:Name="textCreate"
                                   Grid.Row="1"
                                   Text="Create"
                                   FontFamily="Tahoma"
                                   FontSize="19"
                                   HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                   VerticalAlignment="Bottom" />
                    </Grid>
                </Button>

            </StackPanel>
        </Grid>
    </Border>
</Window>
